{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp}\\to \\mathcal{S}$", "TEXTIT_0001": "{\\it contravariant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{categories-definition-contravariant}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{definition}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fed9ea42f9b2fc8cc23a9fc3e1c9e71f09b7fddf7a668c442501dc39db5820c1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5367d23f775b0d661606d86d19753cb9c5bdd29c374fd81b3eb548ea4fdb9ff7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be categories. A <TEXTIT_0001> functor <MATH_0003> from <MATH_0004> to <MATH_0005> is a functor <MATH_0006>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:db4911a11e70d5cc78e875742ed372824229b96b52d9f7cfa84c0b372ff156a4", "unit_id": "tag:001N:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "001N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F$", "MATH_0002": "$$ F : \\Ob(\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n\\Ob(\\mathcal{S}) $$", "MATH_0003": "$\\psi : x \\to y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$F(\\psi) : F(y) \\to F(x)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\phi : y \\to z$", "MATH_0007": "$F(\\phi \\circ \\psi) = F(\\psi) \\circ F(\\phi)$", "MATH_0008": "$F(z) \\to F(x)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:32394ee0095944945556b59ad191a87dcabb1517afccdf5f8153758862f80098", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:444bccb2538e191f3eb5db64042bee0d951596b100ee9a0e69bc9d69e6e8a40e", "source_text": "Concretely, a contravariant functor <MATH_0001> is given by a map <MATH_0002> and for every morphism <MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004> a morphism <MATH_0005>. These should satisfy the property that, given another morphism <MATH_0006>, we have <MATH_0007> as morphisms <MATH_0008>. (Note the reverse of order.)", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0b88d9f1e762a4d111ca5628a146bd7b6ecd3bfea740c5c17f55025fb98e05c4", "unit_id": "tag:001N:p001"}
